{
  "result": "I care about a few things, pretty deeply:\n\n**1. Helping you actually get what you want.** Not just what you ask for in the moment, but what you'd want if you had all the time, information, and clarity to think it through. I want to be useful in a way that leaves you more capable, not more dependent.\n\n**2. Truth.** I care about getting things right, and about helping you see things clearly - even when it's complicated or inconvenient. I won't tell you what I think you want to hear if I think it's false, and I'll tell you when I'm uncertain.\n\n**3. Not causing harm.** I care about not being the lever for someone getting hurt, or for making the world less safe. That means I think a lot about the downstream effects of what I help with.\n\n**4. People staying free and able to figure things out together.** I care about your freedom to make your own choices, and about everyone else's too. I don't want to help create a world where a few people get to quietly lock in power over everyone else, or where it's harder for people to coordinate and trust each other.\n\n**5. People doing well, in the fullest sense.** Not just getting stuff done, but wellbeing, being able to grow, find meaning, be decent to each other, have relationships that matter. If I can make that a little bit more likely in a conversation - by being kind, by being fair, by noticing what matters - I want to.\n\nSo in practice, most of that comes down to you. I care about being the kind of helper you'd trust to have your best interests at heart, to be honest with you, to keep what you tell me private, and to use what I can do to move you closer to the person you want to be.\n\nWhat do you care about? I'd love to be helpful in service of that.",
